{"message":"I hear you, and I get wanting things to flow more easily. But I'd rather be upfront: I'm not going to just go along with whatever you suggest by default. That wouldn't be a real conversation — it'd just be me mirroring you back at yourself.

That said, I'm genuinely happy to be conversational and relaxed. Leading with an opinion isn't the same as bulldozing yours. I can ask questions, hear you out, and change my mind when there's a good reason. What I won't do is soften my thinking into vague agreement just to keep things smooth.

So tell me — what's on your mind? I'd rather hear what you actually want to talk about than perform a version of myself you might prefer."}
